# uhub — outstanding work

State: sources are 0.7.99 (pre-0.8.0) in CMakeLists.txt, build.zig and
build.zig.zon. Latest tag is 0.7.1. The ChangeLog has a 0.8.0 section in
progress.

## Release blockers (0.8.0)
- ChangeLog: the 0.8.0 section is headed "Plugin API (version 4)" but
  PLUGIN_API_VERSION is 7 (src/plugin_api/types.h:29). Reconcile before
  tagging; note that PLUGIN_API_VERSION_MIN is 5, so v5 plugins still load.
- ChangeLog: no entry yet for the HBRI fixes — the secondary U4/U6 now
  survives validation, post-login port updates are gated on a proven address,
  and a changed advertised address re-challenges. This changes what peers see.
- ChangeLog: no entry yet for the UCMD fixes — 0.7.1 advertised the extension
  as "UCM0" (ADC-EXT 3.7 calls it "UCMD") and sent ICMD to every client
  regardless of whether it negotiated the extension. Both are corrected; UCM0
  is still accepted from clients that mirrored the old advertisement.
- Decide whether the opaque plugin-user refactor (below) lands in 0.8.0. It is
  ABI-breaking, so deferring it means waiting for 0.9.0.
- Tag on release.

## Design / refactor
- Make the plugin-facing user type opaque. The plugin ABI still hands plugins a
  fully-laid-out `struct plugin_user` (src/plugin_api/types.h:44 —
  sid/nick/cid/user_agent/addr/credentials), a by-value mirror of the internal
  hub_user. Plugins should instead receive an opaque handle reached through
  accessor functions, so the hub can evolve its user internals without breaking
  the plugin ABI and plugins keep a genuinely limited view of hub internals.

## HBRI
- A NAT-override user cannot use HBRI at all: check_network() (src/core/inf.c)
  returns early on the nat_override path, before the HBRI intent check, so the
  flag is never set. NAT'd IPv4 plus native IPv6 is exactly the dual-stack case
  HBRI targets, so this is worth revisiting.
- A failed or lost ITCP challenge is not retried within a session; the client
  must reconnect. Deliberate — one outstanding challenge per session bounds the
  ITCP-per-INF-update amplification — but revisit if it proves too strict.
- No e2e coverage (test/e2e/); the unit tests in autotest/test_hbri.tcc and
  autotest/test_inf.tcc cover the token primitives and the INF merge only.

## Networking / platform
- Windows socket support — src/network/network.c. uhub is meant to be portable
  to Windows (not a tier-1 platform, though CI now has a windows job).
  net_set_close_on_exec is resolved (deliberate no-op); other WINSOCK paths may
  still need real implementations.

## Cleanup
- Stale FIXME at src/core/hub.c:642 claims HH/WS/NE/OW are missing. They are
  implemented ~50 lines below (hub.c:694-701) and in regserver.c:230-237.
- The long-standing "flood control should be a plugin" FIXME (hub.c:529) keeps
  policy in core that the plugin ABI was built to host. Detection is already
  split from action; the remaining bit is the privileged-chat check.
- Raw ADC status codes are inlined as magic numbers in hub.c — name them.
- Branch sprawl: 27 local and 34 remote branches, mostly unmerged historical
  topic branches (gnutls_work, libevent_work, visual_studio_2010_work, ...).
  Tag-then-delete historical work; delete locals that only mirror origin.

## Resolved since the 0.6.1 assessment (ASSESSMENT.md)
ASSESSMENT.md is pinned to 0.6.1 and is stale on these points:
- Version drift — CMakeLists.txt, build.zig and build.zig.zon now agree.
- Stale release tooling in admin/ — the directory is gone.
- Dockerfile in-tree build — now `cmake -S . -B build`.
- Untested connection.c state machine and TLS — autotest/test_connect.tcc and
  autotest/test_tls.tcc now exist.
- HBRI was undocumented — now covered in doc/architecture.txt and
  doc/uhub.conf.
